{
  "email": "james.oconnor@brightline.example",
  "reason": "Ticket sender reports the orders@ shared mailbox disappeared from Outlook folder list; checking account, devices, and mailbox status per KB-011 quick checks."
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi James, thanks for reporting this. Your account and mailbox look healthy, so the orders@ mailbox is most likely just not reconnected in Outlook yet. Please try these steps: 1) Fully close Outlook and reopen it. Shared mailboxes are added automatically once access is in place. 2) If it still doesn't appear, check whether it shows up in Outlook on the web (Add shared folder or mailbox). 3) If it's still missing, go to File, Account Settings, Change, More Settings, Advanced, and Add, then enter orders@. Please also confirm whether your access to orders@ was recently changed or newly granted. If you were never granted access, the mailbox owner needs to approve it first, and then we can make the change. Reply and let us know what you see, and we'll follow up from there.",
  "internal_note": "Checked lookup_user for user_id 8 (James O'Connor, Operations). Account active, not blocked, no failed logins, password set 2026-09-11. Mailbox 15.2 GB of 50 GB (29.7%), so mailbox-full is not a factor. Device on file: BL-DT-0108. I have no tool to verify the orders@ grant or Send As permission, so I could not confirm whether access exists. Per KB-011, sent user steps: restart Outlook, check OWA, add the mailbox manually. If the user was never granted access, that needs mailbox owner approval, then Tier 2 for the change (KB-006). Awaiting user reply on whether access was granted and whether the mailbox appears after restart. Not escalated yet.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-011"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
